# What must never enter the build context.
#
# The first two lines are the ones that matter. A build context is uploaded
# whole before anything is built, and .env holds this node's Anthropic key,
# Copernicus credentials and SECRET_KEY -- sending that to a build service is
# how a secret ends up in an image layer that outlives the deploy.
.env
.env.*

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Photographs farmers submitted for diagnosis. Never part of an image.
media/

tests/
requirements-dev.txt
pytest.ini

# Kept: models/ is COPYed by the Dockerfile and served over
# /models/{id}/artifact, which is how a peer node obtains this one's disease
# classifier. Excluding it 404s the federation endpoint.
